//
// The design artifacts' FAB (floating action button), the FACE: a 56 px `accent` circle with the
// action's glyph — 22 px, stroke 2.4, `onAccent` — and `shadow2` under it. Hover and press are
// the host's layers over the circle (white 14 % / black 12 % on a filled control).
//
// Handler-free, like `WinButtonFace`: the app owns the tap and the place — a FAB sits 24 px from
// the content's corner (an out-of-flow layer with spacers), and the tap needs a name:
//
//     Stack { WinFabFace { icon: "plus" } }
//     .label(@t("new"))
//     on Tap -> dispatch(NewItem)
//
// The design's speed-dial (the plus turning 45°, minis rising 12 px in 40 ms steps) needs a
// rotation and a staggered transform the DSL does not bind; a FAB with actions opens a
// `WinMenu` above it instead.

Component WinFabFace {
    props: {
        icon: Str,
    }
    Circle { size: 56
        Icon { symbol: $props.icon, size: 22, stroke: 2.4 }
            .fg(onAccent)
    }
    .bg(accent)
    .shadow(shadow2)
}
